<cell id="cell-0"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type># M6 L6: Chunking and Context Preservation

**Build three chunkers, ablate them on a fixed corpus.**

Duration: 90 min.  No API keys.</cell id="cell-0>
<cell id="cell-1"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type>## Plain English (the 12-year-old version)

**Chunking** means cutting a long document into smaller pieces so the search engine can find the right piece quickly.

Imagine a 50-page book. If you search "vacation policy" and the search engine returns the whole book, you have to find the answer yourself. If the book is pre-cut into one-page chapters, the engine can return just the vacation page.

There are three ways to cut: **fixed window** (every 400 characters, like tearing pages evenly), **recursive** (cut at paragraph breaks first, then sentences), and **structure-aware** (keep section headings with their paragraphs). The third way is usually best for organized documents.</cell id="cell-1>
<cell id="cell-2"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type>## The 5 things to know

1. **Chunking is the highest-leverage knob in RAG quality** — 200 vs 800 chars can mean 30 points of recall.
2. **Three families**: fixed window, recursive, structure-aware.
3. **Default pick**: recursive; upgrade to structure-aware if the docs have headings.
4. **Always ablate on your golden set** — not on the textbook.
5. **The four knobs**: chunk_size, overlap, separators, heading awareness.</cell id="cell-2>
<cell id="cell-3"># === Standard setup ===
import sys, importlib.util
from pathlib import Path

def find_root(p):
    while p != p.parent:
        if (p / 'lessons').exists() and (p / 'SYLLABUS.md').exists():
            return p
        p = p.parent
    return Path.cwd()

ROOT = find_root(Path.cwd())
sys.path.insert(0, str(ROOT))

_p = ROOT / 'lessons' / 'm06-chunking' / 'L6-chunking.py'
_spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location('L6', _p)
_L6 = importlib.util.module_from_spec(_spec)
sys.modules['L6'] = _L6
_spec.loader.exec_module(_L6)

print(f'Setup OK. Lesson module: {_L6.LESSON_NUMBER}')</cell id="cell-3>
<cell id="cell-4"># Run the 10 unit tests inline
import inspect
tests = [(n, fn) for n, fn in inspect.getmembers(_L6, inspect.isfunction) if n.startswith('test_')]
print(f'Running {len(tests)} tests...\n')
passed, failed = 0, 0
for name, fn in tests:
    try:
        fn()
        print(f'  PASS  {name}')
        passed += 1
    except AssertionError as e:
        print(f'  FAIL  {name}: {e}')
        failed += 1
print(f'\n{passed}/{len(tests)} tests pass, {failed} fail')
assert failed == 0, f'{failed} test(s) failed -- fix before continuing'</cell id="cell-4>
<cell id="cell-5"># === Section 1: fixed-window chunker ===
fw = _L6.chunk_fixed_window('doc-1', _L6.SAMPLE_TEXT, chunk_size=400, overlap=50)
print(f'n_chunks: {len(fw)}')
for c in fw[:2]:
    print(f'  {c.chunk_id}  chars={len(c.text)}  text={c.text[:60]!r}...')</cell id="cell-5>
<cell id="cell-6"># === Section 2: recursive chunker ===
rc = _L6.chunk_recursive('doc-1', _L6.SAMPLE_TEXT, chunk_size=400, overlap=50)
print(f'n_chunks: {len(rc)}')
for c in rc[:2]:
    print(f'  {c.chunk_id}  chars={len(c.text)}  text={c.text[:60]!r}...')</cell id="cell-6>
<cell id="cell-7"># === Section 3: structure-aware chunker ===
st = _L6.chunk_structure('doc-1', _L6.SAMPLE_TEXT, sentences_per_chunk=5)
print(f'n_chunks: {len(st)}')
for c in st[:2]:
    print(f'  {c.chunk_id}  chars={len(c.text)}  text={c.text[:60]!r}...')</cell id="cell-7>
<cell id="cell-8"># === Section 4: chunk count comparison ===
print('Chunk counts:\n')
print(f'  fixed_window: {len(fw)}')
print(f'  recursive:    {len(rc)}')
print(f'  structure:    {len(st)}')</cell id="cell-8>
<cell id="cell-9"># === Section 5: chunk size distribution ===
print(f'{"chunker":<14} {"mean":>8} {"max":>5} {"min":>5}')
for name, chunks in (('fixed_window', fw), ('recursive', rc), ('structure', st)):
    sizes = [len(c.text) for c in chunks]
    print(f'  {name:<14} {sum(sizes)/len(sizes):>6.1f}  {max(sizes):>4}  {min(sizes):>4}')</cell id="cell-9>
<cell id="cell-10"># === Section 6: ablation (mocked recall) ===
rt = {'fixed_window': 0.62, 'recursive': 0.78, 'structure': 0.85}
rows = _L6.ablation('doc-1', _L6.SAMPLE_TEXT, recall_table=rt)
print(f'{"chunker":<14} {"n_chunks":>9} {"mean":>8} {"max":>5} {"recall@3":>10}')
for r in rows:
    print(f'  {r.chunker:<14} {r.n_chunks:>9} {r.mean_chunk_chars:>8.1f} {r.max_chunk_chars:>5} {r.recall_at_3:>10.2f}')</cell id="cell-10>
<cell id="cell-11"># === Section 7: chunk size sweep on structure ===
print('Sweep sentences_per_chunk on structure chunker:\n')
for spc in (1, 3, 5, 10):
    chunks = _L6.chunk_structure('doc-1', _L6.SAMPLE_TEXT, sentences_per_chunk=spc)
    sizes = [len(c.text) for c in chunks]
    print(f'  spc={spc:>2}  n={len(chunks):>3}  mean={sum(sizes)/max(len(sizes),1):>5.0f} chars')</cell id="cell-11>
<cell id="cell-12"><cell_type>markdown</cell_type>## Architecture (Mermaid)

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    A[document text] --> B{chunker}
    B -->|fixed window| F[split every N chars<br/>with overlap]
    B -->|recursive| R[split on paragraphs<br/>then sentences<br/>then words]
    B -->|structure-aware| S[keep heading as anchor<br/>+ N sentences]
    F --> C[Chunk objects]
    R --> C
    S --> C
    C --> E[embed chunks]
    C --> AB[ablation: compare<br/>recall@K on golden set]
    E --> VDB[vector DB]
    AB --> PICK[pick winner]
```

**Read as:** Chunk first, embed second, ablate always.</cell id="cell-12>
